{"chars": "The twinflower is a little plant that grows in the cool, shady forests of the far north. It creeps along the forest floor on thin green runners, with tiny round leaves that stay green even under the snow. In summer, it sends up a slender stem as thin as a thread. At the top, the stem splits in two, and from each side hangs one small pink bell, nodding down toward the moss. Always two, side by side, like a pair of best friends holding hands. That's why it's called the twinflower. And on a warm summer evening, the twinflower smells sweet, a little like vanilla.", "start": [0.25, 0.25, 0.25, 0.325, 0.325, 0.325, 0.325, 0.325, 0.325, 0.325, 0.325, 0.325, 0.325, 0.325, 0.95, 0.95, 0.95, 1.062, 1.062, 1.113, 1.113, 1.113, 1.113, 1.113, 1.113, 1.113, 1.4, 1.4, 1.4, 1.4, 1.4, 1.4, 1.725, 1.725, 1.725, 1.725, 1.725, 1.85, 1.85, 1.85, 1.85, 1.85, 1.85, 2.212, 2.212, 2.212, 2.288, 2.288, 2.288, 2.288, 2.413, 2.413, 2.413, 2.413, 2.413, 2.825, 2.913, 2.913, 2.913, 2.913, 2.913, 2.913, 3.263, 3.263, 3.263, 3.263, 3.263, 3.263, 3.263, 3.263, 3.712, 3.712, 3.712, 3.788, 3.788, 3.788, 3.788, 3.888, 3.888, 3.888, 3.888, 4.175, 4.175, 4.175, 4.175, 4.175, 4.175, 4.9, 5.0, 5.0, 5.0, 5.125, 5.125, 5.125, 5.125, 5.125, 5.125, 5.125, 5.425, 5.425, 5.425, 5.425, 5.425, 5.425, 5.688, 5.688, 5.688, 5.688, 5.787, 5.787, 5.787, 5.787, 5.787, 5.787, 5.787, 6.175, 6.175, 6.175, 6.175, 6.175, 6.175, 6.463, 6.463, 6.463, 6.638, 6.638, 6.638, 6.638, 6.638, 6.9, 6.9, 6.9, 6.9, 6.9, 6.9, 7.225, 7.225, 7.225, 7.225, 7.225, 7.225, 7.225, 7.225, 7.875, 7.95, 7.95, 7.95, 7.95, 7.95, 8.125, 8.125, 8.125, 8.125, 8.125, 8.45, 8.45, 8.45, 8.45, 8.45, 8.45, 8.75, 8.75, 8.75, 8.75, 8.75, 8.75, 8.75, 9.15, 9.15, 9.15, 9.15, 9.15, 9.275, 9.275, 9.275, 9.275, 9.275, 9.562, 9.562, 9.562, 9.562, 9.562, 9.562, 9.95, 9.95, 9.95, 9.95, 9.95, 10.213, 10.213, 10.213, 10.213, 10.213, 10.213, 10.387, 10.387, 10.387, 10.387, 10.512, 10.512, 10.512, 10.512, 10.512, 11.225, 11.35, 11.35, 11.35, 11.512, 11.512, 11